  "sources": [
    {
      "title": "UniFi Access Point | Releases | Ubiquiti Community",
      "feedUrl": "https://community.ui.com/rss/releases/UniFi-Access-Point-Switch/9fc3b2fa-9e73-449a-924f-470e79884470",
      "siteUrl": "https://community.ui.com",
      "articles": [
        {
          "id": "30619aea-333b-48d3-9753-92f6c5e66a55",
          "author": "UI-Edmundas",
          "description": "Improvements\n\nImproved connectivity.\nImproved stability.\n\nBugfixes\n\nFixed an issue where MLO clients would stop passing traffic when roaming between APs with both MLO and Fast Roaming enabled.\nFixed RADIUS-based MAC authentication so that VLAN assignments are correctly applied on WPA3-Personal networks.\n\nAdditional information\nUpdate your devices by changing the Device Firmware Release Channel in the UniFi Network application to Release Candidate.\n\nIf you wish to go back to the Official release after the upgrade, change the release channel back to Official.\n\nIf you encounter any issues with this release, please provide us with some details on your setup and include the below information:\n\nAP model(s)\nPrevious AP release version\nUniFi Network application version",
          "link": "https://community.ui.com/releases/UniFi-Access-Point-U7-LR-8-0-39/30619aea-333b-48d3-9753-92f6c5e66a55",
          "publishedOn": "2025-06-24T09:45:29.000Z",
          "wordCount": 6,
          "title": "UniFi Access Point (U7-LR) 8.0.39",
          "imageUrl": null
        },
        {
          "id": "d560c28b-8625-4535-938f-a50867597f3b",
          "author": "UI-Edmundas",
          "description": "Overview\nThis release is promoted to Official/Stable release channel for these models:\n\nE7, E7 Campus, E7 Audience - June 26, 2025\nU7 Outdoor, U7 Lite, U7 In-Wall - June 30, 2025\nU7 Pro Max, U7 Pro XG, U7 Pro XGS - July 1, 2025\nU7 Pro, U7 Pro Wall, U7 Pro Outdoor - July 3, 2025\n\nImprovements\n\nAdded Roaming Assistant support\nEnabled wireless meshing for U7/E7 (with MLO enabled) to Wi-Fi 6/5 APs.\nImproved AP stability.\nImproved client connectivity.\nImproved wireless client roaming.\nImproved meshing performance in dense environments.\nImproved airtime utilization on the 5 GHz band.\nImproved MLO throughput in specific scenarios.\nImproved 6GHz auto-channel selection algorithm.\nImproved AFC position acquisition stability and prevented intermittent failures.\nImproved Ethernet stability on E7/U7 10…",
          "link": "https://community.ui.com/releases/UniFi-Access-Point-all-U7-and-E7-models-8-0-49/d560c28b-8625-4535-938f-a50867597f3b",
          "publishedOn": "2025-06-23T20:48:42.000Z",
          "wordCount": 6,
          "title": "UniFi Access Point (all U7 and E7 models) 8.0.49",
          "imageUrl": null
        },
        {
          "id": "1f26d559-7645-4c53-bc11-6b3ad01d516d",
          "author": "UI-Edmundas",
          "description": "Overview\nThis is the initial release for the E7-Audience model.\nAdditional information\nIf you encounter any issues with this release, please provide us with some details on your setup and include the below information:\n\nUniFi Network application version\nUniFi Console Support File (as private attachment)",
          "link": "https://community.ui.com/releases/UniFi-Access-Point-E7-Audience-8-0-47/1f26d559-7645-4c53-bc11-6b3ad01d516d",
          "publishedOn": "2025-06-13T14:59:13.000Z",
          "wordCount": 6,
          "title": "UniFi Access Point (E7-Audience) 8.0.47",
          "imageUrl": null
        }
      ]
    },
